WEBVTT

00:06:28.592 --> 00:06:30.803
I performed for mainly indie audiences,

00:06:30.803 --> 00:06:33.055
so they didn’t know
what the fuck was happening,

00:06:33.055 --> 00:06:34.223
and I liked it that way.

00:06:34.223 --> 00:06:35.224
(Laughter)

00:06:35.641 --> 00:06:37.393
Twerking made me feel empowered.

00:06:37.977 --> 00:06:39.687
It was my secret language;

00:06:39.687 --> 00:06:40.688
my sauce.

00:06:41.605 --> 00:06:43.858
Little did I know
that a couple of years later,

00:06:43.858 --> 00:06:47.445
Miley Cyrus would perform what seemed
like the twerk heard around the world.

00:06:48.195 --> 00:06:49.321
Y’all remember that.

00:06:50.531 --> 00:06:51.740
In 2013,

00:06:51.740 --> 00:06:53.200
within a month of each other,

00:06:53.200 --> 00:06:55.077
I released my debut project,

00:06:55.077 --> 00:06:56.120
“Lizzobangers,”

00:06:56.120 --> 00:06:58.747
and Miley Cyrus released
her project, “Bangerz.”

00:06:59.498 --> 00:07:02.918
That same year, Miley released
the single “We Can’t Stop,”